{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvuT2i2A4Rk9XybYQtpn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the one real failure I could reproduce. Every admin page crashed with `KeyError: 'babel'` whenever Flask-Babel was installed but the app never called `Babel(app)`. Flask-Admin now falls back to untranslated English text in that case, and calling `Babel(app)` still turns translations on as before.\n\n**The change:** it's all in `flask_admin/babel.py`. I added a small `_SafeDomain` class that returns untranslated text when Babel isn't set up. Flask-Admin's own translation domain and the WTForms one now both use it.\n\n**Results:** I reran the example apps with Flask-Babel installed. `simple`, `sqla` (all 23 pages), `bootstrap4`, `babel`, `forms_files_images`, `methodview`, `multiple_admin_instances` and `sqla_association_proxy` now load every page without errors. Six of those were crashing before the fix.\n\nTwo examples still failed, but not because of the code: `custom_layout` and `sqla_custom_inline_forms` raised \"no such table\". Those apps only create their database tables when started directly as a script, which my test skips. If you run them with `python main.py` from their folders, they set the tables up themselves.\n\nTo undo the change, the original file is backed up at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-USER-Desktop-exp1-work-runs--work-6a46be7d44-repo/bacf3f29-0432-43ce-a55c-6bb3af328e7d/scratchpad/babel.py.orig`.\n\nIf you're still seeing a problem, it's something I haven't reproduced. Paste the error or tell me what you run and I'll go straight at it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":69142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":478},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"